%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 22d0308a90dc49ae97395f1b651723b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_05_AlertFatigue
  questionId: TECH-05
  category: 1
  speakerName: Principal Security Architect
  questionText: >-
    Their SOC lead says false positives are so bad that analysts ignore half the alerts. How do you prove you will not add more noise?
  answerOptions:
  - {fileID: 11400001}
  - {fileID: 11400002}
  - {fileID: 11400003}
  - {fileID: 11400004}
--- !u!114 &11400001
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_05_A1
  answerText: >-
    Ask for a sample of noisy alert types and define a proof that measures precision, analyst action, and missed-risk review.
  technicalDelta: 3
  commercialDelta: 1
  rapportDelta: 1
  energyDelta: -1
--- !u!114 &11400002
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_05_A2
  answerText: >-
    Explain that your analytics are higher fidelity and show the marketing benchmark.
  technicalDelta: 1
  commercialDelta: 1
  rapportDelta: -1
  energyDelta: 0
--- !u!114 &11400003
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_05_A3
  answerText: >-
    Admit tuning takes work, then propose a phased rollout with suppression criteria owned by the SOC.
  technicalDelta: 2
  commercialDelta: 0
  rapportDelta: 2
  energyDelta: -1
--- !u!114 &11400004
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_TECH_05_A4
  answerText: >-
    Say the product can replace their existing noisy rules, which should reduce analyst load quickly.
  technicalDelta: -1
  commercialDelta: 2
  rapportDelta: -1
  energyDelta: 1
